<title>UK: Britain welcomes Albright appointment.</title>
<headline>Britain welcomes Albright appointment.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>British Foreign Secretary Malcolm Rifkind on Thursday welcomed the appointment of Madeleine Albright to take over from Warren Christopher as U.S. secretary of state.</p>
<p>&quot;I very much welcome Madeleine Albright's nomination as the next U.S. secretary of state,&quot; Rifkind said in a statement.</p>
<p>&quot;I look forward to working closely with her when...she takes up her appointment next year.&quot;</p>
<p>Albright, currently U.S. ambassador to the United Nations, was appointed on Thursday in a sweeping shake-up by U.S. President Bill Clinton of his national security brain-trust.</p>
